  "comment": "Dialect-pack data (vision 42 D2, K15): each ecosystem's framework conventions for test files, read by repofacts' convention basis. Each pack names the dialect it belongs to and the file extensions its patterns apply to. test_suffixes, test_prefixes and test_infixes match the file's base name; test_dirs are directory segments under which every file of the pack is a test; fixture_names are base names of test-support files a runner loads but does not collect; support_dirs are directory segments under which a pack file that is not a test is test support (fixture); test_dir_prefixes are base-name prefixes that mark a test only under a test directory (Surefire's Test* include, which applies to the test source tree). Sources are each runner's own documented default collection: go test, pytest's python_files, jest's testMatch and vitest's include, PHPUnit's suffix, Maven Surefire's includes, RSpec's pattern, cargo's tests/ target directory. split (R1, RF-M8, pre-registered in docs/bench/readings/repository-facts/roles-r1.md) holds a pack's rules for test code its runner does not collect: a file the pack's test patterns match reads test-support instead of test under one of its dirs (exact segment), dir_prefixes or dir_suffixes (example and documentation suites, a directory the runner skips by default), base_prefixes or base_suffixes (abstract bases, files the tool ignores, base-class names), when dir_prefix_match and only test_dir_prefixes matched (a Test* helper), when needs_test_dir and it lies under no test or tests directory, or, when only test_dirs matched, by a helper stem (test_dir_helper_stems, case-insensitive; test_dir_helper_stem_prefixes; test_dir_helper_suffixes) or a helper subdirectory below the test directory (test_dir_helper_dirs). A pack with no split reads every match test.",
